# Conventional Commits, warn-only for now (see plans/01-monorepo-tooling-setup.md
# §8) — always exits 0 so a non-conventional message never blocks a commit,
# it just prints what commitlint would have flagged. Flip to blocking by
# changing `|| true` to nothing once the team grows.
#
# Husky runs this script with `sh -e`, so a trailing `; exit 0` after a
# failing command never gets reached — `-e` aborts right at the failure.
# `|| true` neutralizes the failure inline instead, which `-e` doesn't treat
# as an abort.
#
# Call the binary directly rather than via `pnpm` — see pre-commit for why.
commitlint --edit "$1" --verbose || true
